ok - dispatch entry: the host reads branch eligibility, the offer rule, and the wake prompt from the Pi branch's own owner
ok - away reports: progress, resolved decisions and captain holds stay parked; terminal outcomes, freed slots and unanswered input hand back
ok - away merge handback: only the exact reported lane receives a derived dispatch
ok - away batched merge: a sibling signal can precede the handed lane, and MAIN receives only its merge handback
ok - away explicit decisions: sibling wakes and terminal events cannot relabel a lane's input handback
ok - away dispatch handback: derived terminal reports collapse per turn and task while explicit actions and outcomes survive
ok - away handback: MAIN work survives engine acknowledgement and a dropped close, then the same posture resumes routine supervision
ok - away worker input reaches MAIN, while explicit captain-owned holds stay for return
ok - away handback: the engine acknowledges other handled lanes first; MAIN drains only the named handback lane
ok - away handback: receipt and pending-row paths preserve all lanes and actions in one reason line
ok - host: an away wake is handled on the engine through the branch contract and never reaches main
ok - host: an engine turn that records no outcome hands its durable wake to main
ok - host: a captain return during an engine turn hands that turn's outcomes to main
ok - host: a turn that reports but leaves its granted rows queued hands the wake to main
ok - host: an attended wake the branch may take is handled on the engine, and its routine outcome never wakes main
ok - host: an attended captain outcome wakes main once and stays in its drain until main acknowledges it
